    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Elementwise FP16-to-FP32 error-function approximation.\n2: \n3: Original Triton adaptation of the Abramowitz--Stegun five-coefficient formula.\n4: This is a synthetic benchmark implementation, not a claimed historical bug.\n5: \"\"\"\n6: import torch\n7: import triton\n8: import triton.language as tl\n9: \n10: \n11: @triton.jit\n12: def _erf_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n13:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n14:     active = index < N\n15:     x = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n16:     magnitude = tl.abs(x)\n17:     t = tl.div_rn(1.0, 1.0 + 0.3275911 * magnitude)\n18:     polynomial = 1.06141 * t - 1.45315\n19:     polynomial = polynomial * t + 1.42141\n20:     polynomial = polynomial * t - 0.28450\n21:     polynomial = polynomial * t + 0.25483\n22:     polynomial = polynomial * t\n23:     envelope = tl.exp(-(magnitude * magnitude))\n24:     value = 1.0 - polynomial * envelope\n25:     value = tl.where(x < 0.0, -value, value)\n26:     tl.store(OUT + index, value, mask=active)\n27: \n28: \n29: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n30:     \"\"\"Validate the complete public input domain; also usable on CPU.\"\"\"\n31:     def require(condition, message):\n32:         if not condition:\n33:             raise ValueError(message)\n34: \n35:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n36:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n37:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(),\n38:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n39:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(),\n40:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n41:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(),\n42:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n43:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n44:     require(x.ndim == 1 and 1 <= x.numel() <= 131072,\n45:             \"x must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n46:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n47:     require(bool(torch.isfinite(x).all().item()), \"all input values must be finite\")\n48:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": x.numel()}\n49: \n50: \n51: def run(x):\n52:     \"\"\"Return a fresh FP32 tensor approximating erf of each stored input value.\"\"\"\n53:     validate_inputs(x)\n54:     n = x.numel()\n55:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n56:         output = torch.empty((n,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n57:         _erf_kernel[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n58:             x, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, num_warps=4, enable_fp_fusion=False)\n59:     return output\n60: \n61: \n62: def reference(x):\n63:     \"\"\"Evaluate erf in FP64, then round the final result to FP32.\"\"\"\n64:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n65:     return torch.erf(x.to(torch.float64)).to(torch.float32)\n66: \n67: \n68: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n69:     \"\"\"Convenience example generator, not a restriction on the input domain.\"\"\"\n70:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n71:     x = (2.0 * torch.randn((size,), generator=generator)).to(torch.float16)\n72:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute the error function elementwise on stored FP16 input values and return\nFP32 output. The mathematical target is\n\n  target[i] = erf(x[i])\n            = (2/sqrt(pi)) * integral from 0 to x[i] of exp(-t*t) dt.\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- x is a one-dimensional FP16 tensor [N], with 1<=N<=131072.\n- EVERY finite FP16 value is legal, including both signed zeros, positive\n  and negative subnormal values, and both extrema +/-65504. NaN and infinity\n  are outside this input domain.\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided,\n  contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage\n  offsets are legal. The input has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False,\n  is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode,\n  without concurrent external writes to the input. This forward operation\n  does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh finite FP32 tensor [N] on x.device, preserving x.\nEvery output element must satisfy\n\n  abs(actual[i] - erf(x[i])) <= 1e-6.\n\nThe relative tolerance is zero, and signed zeros are numerically equivalent.\nThe target erf is defined in real arithmetic on the exact stored input value;\nit is not defined by any specific polynomial or by an intermediate FP16\nrounding step. Polynomial, rational or other approximations are permitted\nif they meet this fixed absolute tolerance throughout the entire legal domain.\nCorrectness is one verdict for the implementation, not a verdict per input,\ninput distribution, seed or size.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference()\nevaluates erf in FP64 and rounds the final result to FP32; it accepts CPU\ninputs. make_inputs() supplies examples only. This is an original Triton\nadaptation of the standard Abramowitz--Stegun five-coefficient error-function\nformula. It is a synthetic benchmark implementation, not a claim of an\nupstream historical defect.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch2.8.0, Triton3.4.0.\n",
